Subject: webrtc: allow deterministic ICE candidate address override

Expose the caller-provided address at WebRTC's native candidate serializer. The
wrapper can pass --fingerprint-webrtc-ip as an explicit launch argument; the
browser forwards it to child processes alongside the existing Apostate profile
switch. It takes one value, an IP literal, and has no "auto" mode: the check
below is for a non-empty string, so any other word would be written into the
SDP verbatim.

This changes only host and server-reflexive SDP candidate text and its related
address, preventing the original local address from remaining in raddr. It
changes nothing about where the packets go. It rewrites a string that WebRTC
computed from a socket, while the socket carries on sending from wherever it
was bound, so on its own it leaves the SDP naming one address and the datagrams
arriving at the far end from another. A remote peer, and so any detector
prepared to answer one connectivity check, reads the real source address off
the packet and never consults the text at all.

Patch 0086 is what closes that: it relays WebRTC's UDP through the configured
SOCKS5 proxy so the address is true rather than substituted, and refuses to
create the socket when the configured proxy cannot carry a datagram. With 0086
in the series this patch is not the mechanism that hides the host address; it
remains available for the narrower job of pinning the text of a candidate to a
chosen literal, which a user who already knows their exit address may want for
consistency across launches.

--- a/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.cc
+++ b/third_party/webrtc/api/candidate.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,9 @@
  */
 
 #include "api/candidate.h"
+#if defined(WEBRTC_CHROMIUM_BUILD)
+#include "base/command_line.h"
+#endif
 
 #include <algorithm>  // IWYU pragma: keep
 #include <cstddef>
@@ -81,19 +84,38 @@
   os << kAttributeCandidate;
 
   absl::string_view type = candidate.type_name();
+  std::string address =
+      candidate.address().ipaddr().IsNil()
+          ? candidate.address().hostname()
+          : candidate.address().ipaddr().ToString();
+  bool address_overridden = false;
+#if defined(WEBRTC_CHROMIUM_BUILD)
+  if (candidate.is_stun() || candidate.is_local()) {
+    const base::CommandLine* command_line =
+        base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
+    if (command_line->HasSwitch("fingerprint-webrtc-ip")) {
+      std::string spoofed_address =
+          command_line->GetSwitchValueASCII("fingerprint-webrtc-ip");
+      if (!spoofed_address.empty()) {
+        address = std::move(spoofed_address);
+        address_overridden = true;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+#endif
   os << kSdpDelimiterColon << candidate.foundation() << " "
      << candidate.component() << " " << candidate.protocol() << " "
      << candidate.priority() << " "
-     << (candidate.address().ipaddr().IsNil()
-             ? candidate.address().hostname()
-             : candidate.address().ipaddr().ToString())
+     << address
      << " " << candidate.address().PortAsString() << " "
      << kAttributeCandidateTyp << " " << type << " ";
 
   // Related address
   if (!candidate.related_address().IsNil()) {
     os << kAttributeCandidateRaddr << " "
-       << candidate.related_address().ipaddr().ToString() << " "
+       << (address_overridden ? address
+                              : candidate.related_address().ipaddr().ToString())
+       << " "
        << kAttributeCandidateRport << " "
        << candidate.related_address().PortAsString() << " ";
   }

--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -2960,6 +2960,7 @@
       // child, which is why the switch belongs here rather than in a
       // per-process-type list.
       ::switches::kApostateProfile,
+      "fingerprint-webrtc-ip",
   };
   command_line->CopySwitchesFrom(browser_command_line, kCommonSwitchNames);
 

